{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4TUAfHStnA932FCQybb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found nothing in payload 2/32 that blocks the release: no P0, no new P1, and none of the declared conditions is false against these files. Decision: GO, with four minor (P2) follow-ups.\n\nThe payload is 12 new files that the decomposition moved out of the old `audit_emit.py`. `install()` then rebinds them to the facade. I couldn't run Python, so the checks below come from reading the code and searching the tree; I did not run the tests.\n\n- **Names resolve:** every name used by these files is defined and exported, with no duplicate definitions that could override each other at install time.\n- **Dispatch keeps old behaviour:** 172 branches across the five groups, and no action appears in two groups. Dropped events still write nothing, and unhandled actions still record only the action name.\n- **Test patch points still work.**\n- **Python:** standard library only, and nothing newer than Python 3.9.\n- **Adopter impact:** the only behaviour change is the two new learning-rail enum values for the Bash indirect guard. They match their producer and the CHANGELOG. No hook decision, model, effort or block path is touched.\n- **Shipping:** `_audit_emit_parts` is on the kernel deny list, and `scripts/install.sh` copies it on fresh installs. `scripts/upgrade.sh` and the SPEC schema file are not in this copy, so I couldn't check the upgrade path or the claimed SPEC enum change.\n\nThe structured output carries the full report, with the checks, a note on one redacted clamp value, and these four P2 follow-ups. The first two are minor, the last two are harmless leftovers:\n- **Prefix check in the pair-rail wrapper:** the typed wrapper cuts the file-path hash prefix to 16 characters before validating it, while the generic path drops an oversized value. The current caller can't reach this.\n- **Stale docstring:** `defense.py` still says \"four\" learning rails; there are now five.\n- **Dead code:** `emit_generic` has two special-case branches that do the same thing as the default path.\n- **Guard rail for `install()`:** it only rebinds plain functions. A test that every exported callable is a function would stop a future part from quietly ignoring test patches."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1885,"cache_read_input_tokens":200092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1885},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6578c450-61c9-4189-b7af-966fbe2564f1","uuid":"9ef88ac3-1642-4b0a-acff-fb2b0ea0c867","timestamp":"2026-11-15T09:13:50.383Z","request_id":"req_011Ch4TUAMBbTtSuBqkMij9G"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4TUAfHStnA932FCQybb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LPyZNXx6EkV75s33Hgki8F","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"SCOPE OF PAYLOAD 2/32: twelve new files under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/ (generic_dispatch_01..05.py, governance.py, harness.py, harness_schemas.py, lifecycle.py, lifecycle_schemas.py, operations.py, optimizer.py). They hold declarations moved out of the former monolithic _lib/audit_emit.py (PLAN-197). install() in _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:20-48 rebinds them to the facade namespace, called from audit_emit.py:413-452. The dispatch tuple and emit_generic are at audit_emit.py:464-480.\n\nWHAT WAS VERIFIED (against the redacted candidate tree; no code was executed)\n1. Moved code, name resolution under install(): every free name used by functions in these files resolves at call time. It is either exported in the __all__ of a module in the install list, or a facade name that exists before any call (_KNOWN_ACTIONS, emit_generic, _GENERIC_DISPATCH_HANDLERS).\n   - The helpers and enums come from writer, tokens_boot, boot_schemas, optimizer, federation_schemas, compaction, context_pressure, confidence, federation_persona, rate_limits, adapters, orchestration, workflow, finalization, lifecycle_schemas and harness_schemas.\n   - Checked one by one: _scrub_ceo_boot_event, _breadcrumb, _write_event, _preview, the clamp/hash helpers, all 29 federation allowlists, the _OPTIMIZER_ALLOWLISTS keys, the learning/ledger/persona/confidence enums, _plan088_rate_admit, _plan088_payload_cap, _ATLAS_REGISTRY, emit_task_route_key_dropped and emit_reality_ledger_key_dropped.\n   - Cross-module references are exported: harness_schemas functions use _LEARNING_ID_RE, _LESSON_SHA256_RE and _EGRESS_DEST_MAX_LEN, all exported by lifecycle_schemas or harness_schemas.\n   - No name defined in these files is also defined in another part, so install()'s later-wins update cannot silently override them.\n2. Import-time safety:\n   - Module level holds only literals, re.compile, and two explicit sibling imports: harness_schemas imports _LEARNING_ENVELOPE from lifecycle_schemas, and optimizer imports _OPTIMIZER_ENVELOPE from boot_schemas. _OPTIMIZER_ENVELOPE is a tuple, so tuple + tuple holds.\n   - No part in the package creates a lock or opens a file at module level, so install()'s deepcopy cannot raise. Compiled patterns deepcopy to themselves on Python 3.7+.\n   - All function defaults in these files are literals.\n3. Dispatch equivalence:\n   - 172 \"action ==\" branches across the five groups (34/45/45/28/20). No action appears in two groups, so first-match order cannot hide a second transform.\n   - The drop branches (persona_coverage_synthesized, tier_policy_loader_fallback_observed, audit_producer_path_pollution_detected) return None, and _dispatch_generic (generic_dispatch_05.py) then returns without writing.\n   - A branch that returns True gets exactly one _write_event. If every group returns False, the event is default-denied: only {\"action\": action} is written, plus a breadcrumb. Unknown actions are dropped with a breadcrumb.\n   - The _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH check runs last. Its disjointness from branched actions is asserted by the partition tests in test_audit_emit_ghost_action_guard.py, which parse the source of _GENERIC_DISPATCH_HANDLERS.\n4. Test patch points:\n   - Rebound functions look names up in the facade globals, so patching audit_emit._write_event, _preview, emit_generic, _KNOWN_ACTIONS or _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH still takes effect (see test_audit_emit_modular_facade.py).\n   - The only surface that patches cannot reach is _GENERIC_DISPATCH_HANDLERS, which captures the handler objects at import time. Those names are new, so no previous patch point is lost.\n5. Python:\n   - Standard library only (re, copy, importlib, types).\n   - typing names appear only in annotations, which stay strings under \"from __future__ import annotations\"; function-local annotations are never evaluated.\n   - No syntax newer than 3.9. FunctionType(code, globals, name, defaults, closure) is valid on 3.9.\n6. Adopter blast radius:\n   - The only change visible in these files is additive. lifecycle_schemas.py:508-516: _LEARNING_RAIL_ENUM gains \"bash_indirect\", and _LEARNING_SWITCH_ENUM gains CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD and CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS.\n   - These match the producer (bash_indirect_telemetry.py:18-21 and 59-65) and the CHANGELOG [1.4.4] entry on SPEC enums. Without them the typed wrapper in defense.py:33-34 would coerce the values to observe/other.\n   - No hook decision, model or effort setting, or blocking path is touched. Nothing in these files writes except through _write_event.\n7. Kernel coverage: \".claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*\" is at check_arbitration_kernel.py:312, consistent with conditions 5 and 7.\n8. Shipping:\n   - scripts/install.sh:1520-1549 copies every top-level _lib entry (directories recursively) except the test harness, so _audit_emit_parts/ reaches fresh installs.\n   - scripts/upgrade.sh is withheld from this tree; the upgrade path belongs to its own payload.\n   - A facade shipped without its parts would make \"import _lib.audit_emit\" raise, and hooks would fail open. That is the declared direction for infrastructure faults, not a defect of this payload.\n\nREDACTION ARTIFACT, NOT A FINDING: generic_dispatch_04.py:266 reads \"min([REDACTED:rg], ...)\" for the chain_length clamp. The same bound is redacted the same way in the comment at actions_extended.py:198. The value cannot be checked from the redacted text.\n\nCONDITIONS AGAINST THIS PAYLOAD: conditions 5 and 7, and the telemetry side of 6, are consistent with the code. None is false.\n\nP0: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n- P2 .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/lifecycle.py:79\n  - Problem: emit_pair_rail_review_expected cuts file_path_hash_prefix to 16 characters before validating it. The isinstance check after the slice is dead, because a non-str value raises TypeError at the slice.\n  - Inconsistency: the generic branch (generic_dispatch_05.py:262-267) validates the raw value and drops oversize values to \"\". So an oversized hex value is emitted as a 16-hex prefix by the typed wrapper but dropped by emit_generic.\n  - Reachability: not reachable today. The producer, _pair_rail_parts/part_04.py:105-107, passes a computed prefix and wraps the call in a fail-open try/except. The code is probably carried over verbatim.\n  - Fix: check isinstance(str) and fullmatch the raw value before any slicing, as review_id already does.\n- P2 .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/defense.py:20-21 (sibling file in the same package)\n  - Problem: the docstring still describes \"the four learning-loop rails (observe / distill / boot_render / fact_gate)\", but lifecycle_schemas.py:508 now lists five, including bash_indirect. The PLAN-154 comment block above that enum has not been updated either.\n  - Fix: update the prose.\n- P2 .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:474-479\n  - Problem: emit_generic has two special-case branches (tool_call_lifecycle_recorded and settings_tamper_detected) that do exactly what the fall-through does. This is dead refactor residue.\n  - Fix: delete them, or comment why they exist.\n- P2 .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:36-48\n  - Problem: install() rebinds only top-level FunctionType exports. A future part that exports a class, a functools.partial or a container of functions would keep the template module's globals and silently bypass patches on the facade. Nothing in this payload does that.\n  - Fix: add a test asserting that every callable a part exports is a plain function that install() rebinds.\n- Not verifiable from this tree: SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md, where the CHANGELOG says the enum values were added, is absent from the reviewer copy (withheld). It is judged in its own payload.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Payload 2/32 only moves the audit_emit declarations into parts that rebind cleanly to the facade, with every name resolved, one transform per action, unchanged drop and default-deny behaviour, standard library only, Python 3.9 compatible, an additive enum change that matches its producer and the CHANGELOG, and no declared condition contradicted and no P0 found."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1885,"cache_read_input_tokens":200092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1885},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6578c450-61c9-4189-b7af-966fbe2564f1","uuid":"31ec6138-eb5b-4629-aa28-17df6defd67a","timestamp":"2026-11-15T09:14:15.494Z","request_id":"req_011Ch4TUAMBbTtSuBqkMij9G","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LPyZNXx6EkV75s33Hgki8F":{"report":"SCOPE OF PAYLOAD 2/32: twelve new files under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/ (generic_dispatch_01..05.py, governance.py, harness.py, harness_schemas.py, lifecycle.py, lifecycle_schemas.py, operations.py, optimizer.py). They hold declarations moved out of the former monolithic _lib/audit_emit.py (PLAN-197). install() in _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:20-48 rebinds them to the facade namespace, called from audit_emit.py:413-452. The dispatch tuple and emit_generic are at audit_emit.py:464-480.\n\nWHAT WAS VERIFIED (against the redacted candidate tree; no code was executed)\n1. Moved code, name resolution under install(): every free name used by functions in these files resolves at call time. It is either exported in the __all__ of a module in the install list, or a facade name that exists before any call (_KNOWN_ACTIONS, emit_generic, _GENERIC_DISPATCH_HAN