selves on Python 3.7+.\\n   - All function defaults in these files are literals.\\n3. Dispatch equivalence:\\n   - 172 \\\"action ==\\\" branches across the five groups (34/45/45/28/20). No action appears in two groups, so first-match order cannot hide a second transform.\\n   - The drop branches (persona_coverage_synthesized, tier_policy_loader_fallback_observed, audit_producer_path_pollution_detected) return None, and _dispatch_generic (generic_dispatch_05.py) then returns without writing.\\n   - A branch that returns True gets exactly one _write_event. If every group returns False, the event is default-denied: only {\\\"action\\\": action} is written, plus a breadcrumb. Unknown actions are dropped with a breadcrumb.\\n   - The _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH check runs last. Its disjointness from branched actions is asserted by the partition tests in test_audit_emit_ghost_action_guard.py, which parse the source of _GENERIC_DISPATCH_HANDLERS.\\n4. Test patch points:\\n   - Rebound functions look names up in the facade globals, so patching audit_emit._write_event, _preview, emit_generic, _KNOWN_ACTIONS or _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH still takes effect (see test_audit_emit_modular_facade.py).\\n   - The only surface that patches cannot reach is _GENERIC_DISPATCH_HANDLERS, which captures the handler objects at import time. Those names are new, so no previous patch point is lost.\\n5. Python:\\n   - Standard library only (re, copy, importlib, types).\\n   - typing names appear only in annotations, which stay strings under \\\"from __future__ import annotations\\\"; function-local annotations are never evaluated.\\n   - No syntax newer than 3.9. FunctionType(code, globals, name, defaults, closure) is valid on 3.9.\\n6. Adopter blast radius:\\n   - The only change visible in these files is additive. lifecycle_schemas.py:508-516: _LEARNING_RAIL_ENUM gains \\\"bash_indirect\\\", and _LEARNING_SWITCH_ENUM gains CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD and CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS.\\n   - These